Conductor CLI updater and task-relevant lessons — acceptance ledger, 2026-09-27

Scope: local installed components, official-source acquisition, ownership, language,
private memory/settings preservation, recoverable update and CLI delivery/removal.
Companion upgrades, project-adapter updates and automatic Cursor UI changes excluded.
This is an implementation acceptance record, not a new whole-project audit.

Observed initial checks:
- Windows updater suite: 32 tests, exit 0, one POSIX symlink test skipped.
- Linux updater suite: 32 tests, exit 0, all executed.
- Windows task recall: 16 tests, exit 0, two symlink privilege cases skipped.
- Windows memory delivery/maintenance: 10 tests, exit 0.
- Windows evidence: 80 tests, exit 0, three platform-specific cases skipped.
- Windows settings JSON: 20 tests, exit 0.

Refutations during implementation:
- Concurrent edit after prepare: assertion FAIL without guarded preflight observations;
  guard now binds the transaction to the earlier bytes. Fresh targeted test exit 0.
- Linux installer mode mismatch: identical content hashes, actual mode 0755 vs recorded
  0644. Registration now records observed installed modes. Fresh installer/update test exit 0.
- Snapshot recovery size: 13 MiB source produced a backup larger than the reader's limit.
  Test failed before fix; oversized backup now refuses before target writes, test exit 0.
- Existing memory tests isolated only CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, not HOME. New launcher delivery
  exposed the incomplete sandbox. Both memory installer fixtures now isolate HOME and
  USERPROFILE. Two newly created test launchers in the real profile were identified by
  exact snapshot hashes and prior absence, then moved into their backup for recovery.
  No pre-existing command was overwritten; no private memory was changed by those tests.

Final affected-suite checks:
- python -B -m unittest discover -s qa/updater -v: Windows 37 tests, exit 0,
  two POSIX cases skipped; Linux 37 tests, exit 0, one Windows case skipped.
- Windows installed-hook verification also passed from PowerShell, where PATH bash
  resolves to WSL; explicit Git Bash selection prevents the observed hook-smoke failure.
- Linux mode-only rollback now restores permissions and refuses later user chmod.
  The original test failed (0644 != 0755). Content-only equality caused the skip;
  the alternative hypothesis (filesystem ignored chmod) was excluded by stat readings.
- Existing memory 10, recall 16, evidence 80, memory restore 14 tests passed on both OSes;
  platform-only cases skipped explicitly. Windows settings JSON 20 tests passed.
- Doctor integration, uninstall 7 scenarios, lint both locales, lint negative self-test
  32/32 and shell syntax passed. These unchanged checks are reused after updater-only fixes.
- Isolated CURRENT copies retained CURRENT tests: preflight edit and backup-size guards,
  rollback permissions and Windows Bash selection each PASS -> assertion FAIL -> PASS.

Live deployment: both installers completed in Russian with companion installation skipped.
213 private file hashes (lessons, curated/project memory, private Git metadata, backup
script and language) were identical before/after; foreign settings preserved. Runtime
and global rules were snapshotted outside the public Git set. Installed conductor status
reports claude/global/values, Russian. Bootstrap revision is null, not a claimed release.

Graph refresh and official-source publication/real CLI update: still in progress at this
record. Do not treat local test fixtures as proof of a published release.
